{
  "name": "OPS.SLK-B Slack Join Provisioner",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## OPS.SLK-B · Slack Join Provisioner\n\nSlack `team_join` event → verify signature → match email in `team_members` → resolve channels from `slack_role_channels` × `slack_market_slugs` → ids from `slack_channels` → (live only) invite, mark row `active`, welcome DM → `#ops-alerts`.\n\n**Answer Slack first.** The Respond node fires before any Supabase or Slack call. Slack retries after 3 s otherwise and you get double provisioning. The URL-verification challenge is answered by the same node.\n\n**Signature check is fail-closed.** `SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET` unset, timestamp older than 5 min, or HMAC mismatch → 401 and nothing runs. The HMAC is computed by the Crypto node (the Code sandbox cannot require('crypto')); the raw request body comes from the Webhook node's Raw Body option — do not turn it off.\n\n**`SLACK_ONBOARDING_MODE`** — anything but `live` is shadow: full evaluation, then one `[SHADOW]` line in #ops-alerts naming exactly what would happen. No invites, no channel, no DB update. Flipping to live is Mark's separate decision.\n\n**No role logic here.** Canvassers never see #dispatch because `slack_role_channels` has no such row, not because of an IF.\n\n**Alerts you will see:** 🔴 UNKNOWN JOIN (no form row) · 🔴 DEPARTED REJOIN (row is departed, nothing provisioned) · 🟠 MISSING CHANNEL / NO ROLE MAPPING / UNKNOWN MARKET (data gaps, the rest still proceeds) · ✅ ONBOARDED.\n\n**Idempotent-ish.** already_in_channel counts as success, so re-running never double-invites.\n\n**No per-rep channels (2026-09-14).** Reps land in their market's `#sales-<market>` channel, which the role patterns already grant. Nothing here creates a private channel.\n\n`Resolve Channels` embeds `scripts/lib/slack-onboarding-resolve.js` verbatim — the test suite checks it.",
        "height": 660,
        "width": 820,
        "color": 4
      },
